.DS_Store
build/
build-*/
.cache/
# ...and `.cache` itself, without the slash. A trailing slash matches a *directory* only, so an
# agent worktree whose `.cache` is a symlink to the main checkout's cache was not ignored, was
# committed, and merging it back replaced this checkout's real 560 MB cache with a symlink pointing
# at itself. Cost a full dependency restore to undo.
.cache
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
cmake-build-*/

# Asset library: CC0 downloads, reproducible with tools/fetch_polyhaven.py. The manifest and the
# fetcher are committed; ~110 MB of textures and meshes are not.
/assets/nature/
/assets/terrain/
/assets/quaternius
# Skies (ADR-049): the .hdr files are hundreds of megabytes; assets/hdri/manifest.json records
# which ones and at what resolution, and the fetcher restores them.
/assets/hdri/*.hdr

# Generated benchmark scene variants (tools/make_bench_scenes.py); derived from
# examples/world/terrain.scene.json
/examples/world/_bench/
# Score (assets/audio/manifest.json): generated by tools/make_glowmere_score.py, deterministic
# down to the byte, and 16 MB. The manifest carries the command and the hash; the wav does not
# belong in history any more than a build output does.
/assets/audio/*.wav

# The city, character and concert packs (assets/city.manifest.json, ADR-none): 700+ meshes and
# their texture atlases, imported 2026-09-11 for the music video. Gitignored for size, not for
# licence -- both Kenney and Quaternius are CC0, and assets/imported/ATTRIBUTION.md records where
# every one came from and which two have terms nobody has confirmed. The manifest is the part the
# repository keeps: it is the curation and the art direction, and it is what a scene names.
/assets/kenney/city/
/assets/quaternius/street/
/assets/imported/concert/
/assets/imported/instruments/
/examples/world/_flicker_*.scene.json

# The modular aliens (ADR-192): six variants exported from a source .blend that is not in this
# repository. The licence question is settled -- CC0 1.0, recorded in the pack's ATTRIBUTION.md on
# the owner's statement (2026-09-15) -- so what keeps them out now is only the 27 MB. assets/aliens/ATTRIBUTION.md is the part the repository keeps:
# what was dropped and why, the variant table, the two engine limitations the export works within,
# and the one command that regenerates all six (tools/make_aliens.sh). The scenes name the files;
# a worktree without them loads the squad as a bare plinth and says so per missing asset.
/assets/aliens/*.glb

# The farm animals (ADR-205): nine animals exported from a source .blend that is not in this
# repository. 2.5 MB. The licence that kept them out is settled -- CC0 1.0, recorded in the pack's
# ATTRIBUTION.md on the owner's statement (2026-09-15) -- and at 2.5 MB the size was never the
# reason, so they are tracked now. assets/farm/ATTRIBUTION.md is
# the part the repository keeps: the inventory, the three animals that needed handling, the two
# warnings that are harmless and why, and the one command that regenerates all nine
# (tools/make_farm_animals.sh). assets/farm.manifest.json is the other part: it names all nine with
# their real metre sizes, and it resolves whether or not the meshes are on disk.

# Render evidence produced for a change's review (ADR-246's movies and stills, and whatever the
# next one needs). 80 MB for one feature and regenerable from the queue file beside it, which is
# the part worth keeping -- so the queue is committed with the ADR and the pixels are not.
/renders/

# Quality Lab run outputs (ADR-250, mandate §36). A 300-frame 1080p PNG pair plus AOVs is several
# gigabytes; the manifest and metrics.json are the durable record and are small, and the frames are
# reproducible from them plus the git commit. Never committed, for the reason tools/certify.py
# already states: a renderer upgrade changes pixels on purpose.
/quality-results/
# ...and the same frames when a Quality Lab render lands beside its scene. `--render out/candidate`
# is resolved against the PROJECT file's directory, not the working directory (RenderJob takes
# `absolute(projectFile).parent_path()` as its base), so the README's recipe writes 119 MB into
# `examples/quality/out/` and not into the repository root. Same rule, same reason.
/examples/quality/out/
/examples/world/out/

# Staged sources for the published handbook artifact (regenerate rather than commit)
.avgen-manual/
